      "content": "i get the \"long run\" argument but for a lot of us, the short run is just going out of business. it's hard to see how \"leveling the playing field\" helps when a huge corp can just write off the compliance costs as a rounding error while it wipes out my margins. isn't it true that these regulations basically favor big players who can afford the lawyers and new tech, and hurt the little guys more?",
